# terraform.tfstate holds the connector app's client secret in PLAINTEXT —
# marking an output `sensitive` only hides it from console/log output, it
# does NOT encrypt state at rest. Never commit state locally; use a remote
# backend with encryption at rest (see README.md) for anything beyond a
# one-off local run.
#
# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored — commit it. It pins
# exact provider versions/hashes so `terraform init` is reproducible; it
# holds no secrets.
.terraform/
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.backup
terraform.tfvars
*.tfplan
